{"meta":{"templateCredsSetupCompleted":false},"name":"Track customer commitments from Gmail with AI and Google Sheets","tags":[],"nodes":[{"id":"node-01","name":"Sticky Note — Overview","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-1600,-620],"parameters":{"color":4,"width":700,"height":760,"content":"# Customer Promise Control Tower\n\nTurn promises made in customer emails into accountable work before they are missed.\n\nThis workflow scans **sent customer emails**, uses your chosen AI model to identify explicit commitments, and records the promise, owner, customer, due date, confidence, and source message in Google Sheets. A daily control run sends the owner a reminder for commitments due soon or overdue.\n\n## What it protects\n\n- Quotes, documents, callbacks, fixes, approvals, updates, samples, and delivery confirmations that someone said they would send or complete.\n- Customer trust, renewals, revenue, and team accountability.\n\n## Safety model\n\nThe workflow never sends a message to the customer. Low-confidence detections go to **Needs review**. Every record keeps its source-message ID, and Gmail receives a processed label so the same sent email is not assessed twice.\n\n## Before activation\n\nConfigure the yellow Set Template Fields node, create the Google Sheets headers listed there, connect Gmail, Google Sheets, and an OpenRouter HTTP Header Auth credential, then test with one sent customer email."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-02","name":"Sticky Note — Configure first","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-840,-620],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":590,"height":420,"content":"## Configure before activation\n\nUse **Set Template Fields** as the single place to set:\n\n- Your company domain(s) and the Gmail search query.\n- Google Sheets ID, Commitment Register tab, and recipient emails.\n- Reminder window, escalation delay, and confidence threshold.\n- The AI model available through your OpenRouter credential.\n\nCreate a Gmail label named `n8n-commitment-tracked` before running the scan. The workflow adds this label after it assesses each sent message, including messages that contain no commitment.\n\nUse a dedicated inbox or a restricted Gmail query while testing."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-03","name":"Sticky Note — Scan sent customer email","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-220,-620],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":520,"height":280,"content":"## 1. Scan only external sent messages\n\nAn hourly schedule searches Gmail Sent Mail. Internal, automated, and empty messages are excluded before AI is used.\n\nThe Message ID is the idempotency key. Keep the processed-label filter in the Gmail query so already assessed emails are never scanned again."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-04","name":"Sticky Note — Extract commitments with AI","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[330,-620],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":560,"height":280,"content":"## 2. Extract only explicit commitments\n\nThe AI receives the sent message and returns structured JSON. It must identify an action, the exact promise, the customer, the owner, a due date when stated, and confidence.\n\nUse any OpenRouter-supported model. The template is model-neutral and does not depend on a specific provider model."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-05","name":"Sticky Note — Create a durable register","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[920,-620],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":640,"height":300,"content":"## 3. Write a source-backed commitment record\n\nEach qualifying message becomes one Google Sheets row. Records are marked **Open** when confident, or **Needs review** when a due date is unclear or confidence is below the threshold.\n\nThe source message ID and Gmail thread ID make every promise traceable. The owner is notified internally; the customer is never contacted by this workflow."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-06","name":"Sticky Note — Daily promise control","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[360,470],"parameters":{"color":6,"width":650,"height":290,"content":"## 4. Remind before a promise breaks\n\nEvery weekday morning, the workflow reads open commitments. It sends the owner one concise action list for commitments due within the configured window and escalates overdue commitments to the manager.\n\nTo close or reschedule a promise, update its Status or Due Date directly in Google Sheets."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-07","name":"Sticky Note — Privacy and review","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[1620,-620],"parameters":{"color":6,"width":460,"height":280,"content":"## Privacy and human control\n\nOnly grant access to the mailbox that should be monitored. Exclude personal, internal, and automated mail through the Gmail query and domain settings.\n\nAI classification is advisory. Review low-confidence records. Do not use this workflow to automatically make, change, or send customer commitments."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-08","name":"Manual Scan Test","type":"n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger","position":[-900,80],"parameters":{},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"node-09","name":"Hourly Sent Email Scan","type":"n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger","position":[-900,230],"parameters":{"rule":{"interval":[{"field":"cronExpression","expression":"5 * * * *"}]}},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"node-10","name":"Set Scan Mode","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[-650,150],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"scan-mode","name":"executionMode","type":"string","value":"scan"}]},"includeOtherFields":true},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"node-11","name":"Daily Promise Control","type":"n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger","position":[-900,780],"parameters":{"rule":{"interval":[{"field":"cronExpression","expression":"0 8 * * 1-5"}]}},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"node-12","name":"Set Reminder Mode","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[-650,780],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"reminder-mode","name":"executionMode","type":"string","value":"reminder"}]},"includeOtherFields":true},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"node-13","name":"Set Template Fields","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[-670,430],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"internal-domains","name":"internalDomains","type":"string","value":"yourcompany.com"},{"id":"gmail-query","name":"gmailSearchQuery","type":"string","value":"in:sent newer_than:2h -label:n8n-commitment-tracked"},{"id":"gmail-label","name":"processedGmailLabel","type":"string","value":"n8n-commitment-tracked"},{"id":"sheet-id","name":"commitmentSheetId","type":"string","value":"YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID"},{"id":"sheet-tab","name":"commitmentsSheetTab","type":"string","value":"Commitments"},{"id":"owner-fallback","name":"defaultOwnerEmail","type":"string","value":"user@example.com"},{"id":"reviewer-email","name":"reviewerEmail","type":"string","value":"user@example.com"},{"id":"manager-email","name":"managerEmail","type":"string","value":"user@example.com"},{"id":"model","name":"aiModel","type":"string","value":"openai/gpt-4.1-mini"},{"id":"confidence","name":"minimumConfidence","type":"number","value":0.8},{"id":"due-window","name":"reminderWindowHours","type":"number","value":24},{"id":"escalation-days","name":"escalateAfterDays","type":"number","value":1},{"id":"timezone","name":"timezone","type":"string","value":"America/Toronto"}]},"includeOtherFields":true},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"node-14","name":"Is Daily Reminder Run","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[-410,430],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"strict"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"is-reminder","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.executionMode }}","rightValue":"reminder"}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"node-15","name":"Search Sent Customer Emails","type":"n8n-nodes-base.gmail","position":[-130,150],"parameters":{"filters":{"q":"={{ $json.gmailSearchQuery }}"},"options":{},"resource":"message","operation":"getAll","returnAll":true},"typeVersion":2.1},{"id":"node-16","name":"Prepare Sent Customer Messages","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[120,150],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Prepare sent customer messages.\n// Keeps only customer-facing sent emails and carries configuration forward.\nconst config = $input.first().json || {};\nconst internalDomains = String(config.internalDomains || '').split(',').map(v => v.trim().toLowerCase()).filter(Boolean);\nconst results = [];\n\nfunction emailList(value) {\n  return String(value || '').match(/[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z]{2,}/ig) || [];\n}\nfunction header(item, name) {\n  const headers = item.json?.payload?.headers || item.json?.headers || [];\n  const match = Array.isArray(headers) ? headers.find(h => String(h.name || '').toLowerCase() === name.toLowerCase()) : null;\n  return String(match?.value || item.json?.[name.toLowerCase()] || item.json?.[name] || '');\n}\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const j = item.json || {};\n  const to = header(item, 'To') || j.to || '';\n  const cc = header(item, 'Cc') || j.cc || '';\n  const recipients = [...new Set([...emailList(to), ...emailList(cc)].map(v => v.toLowerCase()))];\n  const externalRecipients = recipients.filter(email => !internalDomains.some(domain => email.endsWith('@' + domain)) && !/^(no-?reply|mailer-daemon)@/i.test(email));\n  const body = String(j.textPlain || j.text || j.snippet || j.body?.data || '').trim();\n  const messageId = String(j.id || j.messageId || '').trim();\n  if (!messageId || !externalRecipients.length || body.length < 12) continue;\n  results.push({ json: {\n    ...config,\n    messageId,\n    threadId: String(j.threadId || ''),\n    sentAt: String(j.internalDate || j.date || new Date().toISOString()),\n    senderEmail: header(item, 'From') || String(j.from || config.defaultOwnerEmail || ''),\n    customerEmails: externalRecipients,\n    customerEmail: externalRecipients[0] || '',\n    subject: header(item, 'Subject') || String(j.subject || ''),\n    messageBody: body,\n    sourceLink: 'https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/' + encodeURIComponent(messageId),\n  }});\n}\nreturn results;"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"node-17","name":"Build Commitment AI Request","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[380,150],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Build a model-neutral OpenRouter request without storing an API key.\nconst instruction = String.raw`You identify explicit commitments made by a company to a customer in a sent email. Return ONLY JSON with this exact schema:\n{\n  \"message_id\":\"string copied exactly\",\n  \"contains_customer_commitment\":true,\n  \"commitment_action\":\"short actionable description or empty string\",\n  \"exact_commitment\":\"verbatim promise sentence or empty string\",\n  \"customer_email\":\"email from the provided list or empty string\",\n  \"owner_email\":\"sender email or empty string\",\n  \"due_date\":\"YYYY-MM-DD or null\",\n  \"due_time\":\"HH:mm or null\",\n  \"confidence\":0.0,\n  \"reason\":\"short explanation\"\n}\nRules: A commitment is an explicit future action, delivery, answer, callback, fix, quote, document, approval, or update promised to a customer. Do not treat greetings, vague courtesy, questions, marketing, or a request for customer action as commitments. Resolve relative dates using the sent timestamp. Never invent a date.`;\n\nreturn $input.all().map(item => {\n  const j = item.json || {};\n  return { json: {\n    ...j,\n    aiRequestBody: {\n      model: j.aiModel,\n      temperature: 0,\n      response_format: { type: 'json_object' },\n      messages: [{ role: 'user', content: instruction + '\\n\\nMessage ID: ' + j.messageId + '\\nSent at: ' + j.sentAt + '\\nSender: ' + j.senderEmail + '\\nCustomer emails: ' + j.customerEmails.join(', ') + '\\nSubject: ' + j.subject + '\\n\\nEmail body:\\n' + j.messageBody }],\n    },\n  }};\n});"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"node-18","name":"Extract Commitments with AI","type":"n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest","position":[650,150],"parameters":{"url":"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions","method":"POST","options":{"timeout":60000,"batching":{"batch":{"batchSize":1,"batchInterval":1000}},"response":{"response":{"responseFormat":"json"}}},"jsonBody":"={{ JSON.stringify($json.aiRequestBody) }}","sendBody":true,"specifyBody":"json","authentication":"genericCredentialType","genericAuthType":"httpHeaderAuth"},"typeVersion":4.2},{"id":"node-19","name":"Normalize Commitment Extraction","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[930,150],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Restore context after HTTP Request using the unique source message ID.\nconst responses = $input.all();\nlet sources = [];\ntry { sources = $('Build Commitment AI Request').all(); } catch (error) {}\nconst results = [];\nfor (const response of responses) {\n  let extraction = {};\n  let parseError = '';\n  try {\n    const raw = response.json?.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || response.json?.output || response.json;\n    extraction = typeof raw === 'string' ? JSON.parse(raw.replace(/^\\u0060\\u0060\\u0060json\\s*/i, '').replace(/\\u0060\\u0060\\u0060$/i, '').trim()) : raw;\n  } catch (error) { parseError = String(error.message || error); }\n  const messageId = String(extraction?.message_id || '');\n  const source = sources.find(item => String(item.json?.messageId || '') === messageId);\n  if (!source) continue;\n  const confidence = Number(extraction?.confidence);\n  const containsCommitment = extraction?.contains_customer_commitment === true;\n  const dueDate = String(extraction?.due_date || '').trim();\n  const status = !containsCommitment ? 'Ignored' : (parseError || !dueDate || !Number.isFinite(confidence) || confidence < Number(source.json.minimumConfidence || 0.8) ? 'Needs review' : 'Open');\n  results.push({ json: {\n    ...source.json,\n    containsCommitment,\n    commitmentAction: String(extraction?.commitment_action || '').trim(),\n    exactCommitment: String(extraction?.exact_commitment || '').trim(),\n    extractedCustomerEmail: String(extraction?.customer_email || source.json.customerEmail || '').trim(),\n    ownerEmail: String(extraction?.owner_email || source.json.senderEmail || source.json.defaultOwnerEmail || '').trim(),\n    dueDate: dueDate && dueDate !== 'null' ? dueDate : '',\n    dueTime: String(extraction?.due_time || '').trim(),\n    confidence: Number.isFinite(confidence) ? confidence : 0,\n    extractionReason: String(extraction?.reason || parseError || '').trim(),\n    status,\n    commitmentId: String(source.json.messageId || '') + '::customer-promise',\n  }});\n}\nreturn results;"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"node-20","name":"Label Assessed Gmail Messages","type":"n8n-nodes-base.gmail","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[1190,40],"parameters":{"options":{},"labelIds":"={{ $json.processedGmailLabel }}","resource":"message","messageId":"={{ $json.messageId }}","operation":"addLabels"},"typeVersion":2.1},{"id":"node-21","name":"Is Customer Commitment","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[1190,210],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"strict"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"is-commitment","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.containsCommitment }}","rightValue":true}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"node-22","name":"Prepare Commitment Register Row","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[1450,210],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Create a clean, source-backed row for the Commitment Register.\nreturn $input.all().map(item => {\n  const j = item.json || {};\n  return { json: {\n    'Commitment ID': j.commitmentId || '',\n    'Status': j.status || 'Needs review',\n    'Created At': new Date().toLocaleString('en-CA', { timeZone: j.timezone || 'America/Toronto' }),\n    'Due Date': j.dueDate || '',\n    'Due Time': j.dueTime || '',\n    'Owner Email': j.ownerEmail || j.defaultOwnerEmail || '',\n    'Customer Email': j.extractedCustomerEmail || j.customerEmail || '',\n    'Commitment Action': j.commitmentAction || '',\n    'Exact Commitment': j.exactCommitment || '',\n    'Confidence': j.confidence ?? 0,\n    'Review Reason': j.extractionReason || '',\n    'Source Subject': j.subject || '',\n    'Source Message ID': j.messageId || '',\n    'Source Thread ID': j.threadId || '',\n    'Source Link': j.sourceLink || '',\n    'Last Reminder At': '',\n    'Escalated At': '',\n  }};\n});"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"node-23","name":"Append Commitment Register","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[1720,210],"parameters":{"columns":{"value":{},"schema":[],"mappingMode":"autoMapInputData","matchingColumns":[]},"options":{},"operation":"append","sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"={{ $(\"Set Template Fields\").first().json.commitmentsSheetTab }}"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"={{ $(\"Set Template Fields\").first().json.commitmentSheetId }}"}},"typeVersion":4.6},{"id":"node-24","name":"Restore Commitment Context","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[1980,210],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Google Sheets replaces the input; restore the source record by Commitment ID.\nlet prepared = [];\ntry { prepared = $('Prepare Commitment Register Row').all(); } catch (error) {}\nconst results = [];\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const key = String(item.json?.['Commitment ID'] || '');\n  const source = prepared.find(entry => String(entry.json?.['Commitment ID'] || '') === key);\n  if (source) results.push({ json: { ...source.json } });\n}\nreturn results;"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"node-25","name":"Needs Human Review","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[2230,210],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"strict"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"needs-review","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json[\"Status\"] }}","rightValue":"Needs review"}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"node-26","name":"Send Owner Commitment Notice","type":"n8n-nodes-base.gmail","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[2490,290],"parameters":{"sendTo":"={{ $json[\"Owner Email\"] }}","message":"=A customer commitment was added to the register.\n\nCustomer: {{ $json[\"Customer Email\"] }}\nAction: {{ $json[\"Commitment Action\"] }}\nDue: {{ $json[\"Due Date\"] || \"Review required\" }} {{ $json[\"Due Time\"] }}\nSource: {{ $json[\"Source Link\"] }}\n\nUpdate Status to Fulfilled, Rescheduled, or Cancelled in Google Sheets when complete.","options":{"senderName":"Customer Promise Control Tower","appendAttribution":false},"subject":"=Promise tracked — {{ $json[\"Commitment Action\"] || \"Customer follow-up\" }}","emailType":"text"},"typeVersion":2.1},{"id":"node-27","name":"Send Reviewer Notice","type":"n8n-nodes-base.gmail","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[2490,120],"parameters":{"sendTo":"={{ $(\"Set Template Fields\").first().json.reviewerEmail }}","message":"=A possible customer commitment needs review before it is treated as Open.\n\nAction: {{ $json[\"Commitment Action\"] || \"Not clear\" }}\nExact wording: {{ $json[\"Exact Commitment\"] }}\nConfidence: {{ $json.Confidence }}\nReason: {{ $json[\"Review Reason\"] }}\nSource: {{ $json[\"Source Link\"] }}\n\nSet Status and Due Date in the Commitment Register after review.","options":{"senderName":"Customer Promise Control Tower","appendAttribution":false},"subject":"=Promise review required — {{ $json[\"Customer Email\"] }}","emailType":"text"},"typeVersion":2.1},{"id":"node-28","name":"Read Commitment Register","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[130,780],"parameters":{"options":{},"sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"={{ $json.commitmentsSheetTab }}"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"={{ $json.commitmentSheetId }}"}},"typeVersion":4.6},{"id":"node-29","name":"Prepare Daily Promise Actions","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[400,780],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Build one action list per owner from open or overdue commitment rows.\nconst rows = $input.all().map(item => item.json || {});\nlet config = {};\ntry { config = $('Set Template Fields').first().json || {}; } catch (error) {}\nconst now = new Date();\nconst windowMs = Number(config.reminderWindowHours || 24) * 60 * 60 * 1000;\nconst escalateMs = Number(config.escalateAfterDays || 1) * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\nconst groups = new Map();\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const status = String(row.Status || '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  if (!['open', 'rescheduled'].includes(status)) continue;\n  const dueDate = String(row['Due Date'] || '').trim();\n  if (!dueDate) continue;\n  const due = new Date(dueDate + 'T' + (String(row['Due Time'] || '').trim() || '17:00') + ':00');\n  if (Number.isNaN(due.getTime()) || due.getTime() > now.getTime() + windowMs) continue;\n  const overdue = due.getTime() < now.getTime();\n  const escalated = overdue && (now.getTime() - due.getTime() >= escalateMs);\n  const owner = String(row['Owner Email'] || config.defaultOwnerEmail || '').trim() || config.defaultOwnerEmail;\n  const key = escalated ? String(config.managerEmail || owner) : owner;\n  if (!groups.has(key)) groups.set(key, { recipient: key, escalated, entries: [] });\n  groups.get(key).entries.push({ ...row, overdue, due });\n}\nif (!groups.size) return [];\nreturn [...groups.values()].map(group => ({ json: {\n  ...config,\n  recipient: group.recipient,\n  escalated: group.escalated,\n  actionCount: group.entries.length,\n  actionList: group.entries.map(entry => (entry.overdue ? 'OVERDUE' : 'DUE SOON') + ' | ' + entry['Due Date'] + ' ' + (entry['Due Time'] || '') + ' | ' + entry['Customer Email'] + ' | ' + entry['Commitment Action'] + ' | ' + entry['Source Link']).join('\\n'),\n}}));"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"node-30","name":"Send Daily Promise Action List","type":"n8n-nodes-base.gmail","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[680,780],"parameters":{"sendTo":"={{ $json.recipient }}","message":"=Customer Promise Control Tower action list\n\n{{ $json.actionList }}\n\nUpdate each completed promise to Fulfilled in the Commitment Register. This workflow never contacts customers automatically.","options":{"senderName":"Customer Promise Control Tower","appendAttribution":false},"subject":"={{ $json.escalated ? \"Escalated customer commitments\" : \"Customer commitments due soon\" }} — {{ $json.actionCount }} item(s)","emailType":"text"},"typeVersion":2.1}],"active":false,"pinData":{},"settings":{"timezone":"America/Toronto","callerPolicy":"workflowsFromSameOwner","availableInMCP":false,"executionOrder":"v1","saveManualExecutions":true,"saveExecutionProgress":true,"saveDataErrorExecution":"all","saveDataSuccessExecution":"none"},"versionId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002","connections":{"Set Scan Mode":{"main":[[{"node":"Set Template Fields","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Manual Scan Test":{"main":[[{"node":"Set Scan Mode","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Set Reminder Mode":{"main":[[{"node":"Set Template Fields","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Needs Human Review":{"main":[[{"node":"Send Reviewer Notice","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Send Owner Commitment Notice","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Set Template Fields":{"main":[[{"node":"Is Daily Reminder Run","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Daily Promise Control":{"main":[[{"node":"Set Reminder Mode","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Is Daily Reminder Run":{"main":[[{"node":"Read Commitment Register","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Search Sent Customer Emails","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Hourly Sent Email Scan":{"main":[[{"node":"Set Scan Mode","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Is Customer Commitment":{"main":[[{"node":"Prepare Commitment Register Row","type":"main","index":0}],[]]},"Read Commitment Register":{"main":[[{"node":"Prepare Daily Promise Actions","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Append Commitment Register":{"main":[[{"node":"Restore Commitment Context","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Restore Commitment Context":{"main":[[{"node":"Needs Human Review","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Build Commitment AI Request":{"main":[[{"node":"Extract Commitments with AI","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Extract Commitments with AI":{"main":[[{"node":"Normalize Commitment Extraction","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Search Sent Customer Emails":{"main":[[{"node":"Prepare Sent Customer Messages","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Prepare Daily Promise Actions":{"main":[[{"node":"Send Daily Promise Action List","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Prepare Sent Customer Messages":{"main":[[{"node":"Build Commitment AI Request","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Normalize Commitment Extraction":{"main":[[{"node":"Label Assessed Gmail Messages","type":"main","index":0},{"node":"Is Customer Commitment","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Prepare Commitment Register Row":{"main":[[{"node":"Append Commitment Register","type":"main","index":0}]]}}}